<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Breaking news from AFRICA, Maghreb and Sub-Saharan Africa - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24’s coverage of events, politics and social issues across Africa, including North Africa (the Maghreb) and the Sahel, aided by our network of correspondents and experts across the continent.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/africa/rss</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:59:46Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Across Africa: Tunisians drawn into Russia's war with Ukraine</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c60e3d5ac282879ade3769a3012441ea7cf74110dfdc191a999febcf13f9f5fa</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:59:43Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T21:26:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/across-africa-tunisians-drawn-into-russia-s-war-with-ukraine--2bb5ce40b16f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/across-africa-tunisians-drawn-into-russia-s-war-with-ukraine" /><summary type="html">This week: A new report says more than 1,400 Africans have been recruited to fight for Russia in Ukraine since 2023. Also, as South Africa races to become Africa's digital gateway, a growing backlash is emerging in Cape Town. And music, dance and theatre lit up Abéché as the city's arts festival in Chad drew crowds of young spectators.</summary><category term="Across Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Ngo criticizes UN's response to massacre in South Sudan</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e4e9b3f7c6ab8fe22a13f16c16388ec54ceae26a7979bb5ae3b04123568f2eee</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:59:46Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T21:20:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/ngo-criticizes-un-s-response-to-massacre-in-south-sudan--2191e46554fc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/ngo-criticizes-un-s-response-to-massacre-in-south-sudan" /><summary type="html">In tonight's edition, Amnesty International accuses both the government and UN peacekeepers of failing to protect civilians during a massacre in South Sudan that killed over 200 people. Also, more than a thousand people are prosecuted for illegal mining in Guinea. And a century after French colonial troops killed him, a Malagasy king has finally come home.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>DR Congo's Tshisekedi signs referendum law amid fears of third-term bid</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b5e52d6f64ef7ddd368625343587347e8fb0de016f3fb5865d5e1c322d1dbe21</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:58:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T10:51:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261112-dr-congo-s-tshisekedi-signs-referendum-law-amid-fears-of-third-term-bid--27073301dc67.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261112-dr-congo-s-tshisekedi-signs-referendum-law-amid-fears-of-third-term-bid" /><summary type="html">DR Congo President Félix Tshisekedi paved the way for a constitutional amendment on November 10 by signing a law authorising a referendum. The move comes amid concerns that he could seek a third term in office, with opposition figures accusing him of manoeuvring to remain in power.</summary></entry><entry><title>Kenya discharges last Ebola patient, 42-day countdown to 'Ebola-free' begins</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0cac3347d80c7a3a306c0161870405ce8704208dc546fed22a998c15ac992431</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:58:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T10:48:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261112-kenya-discharges-last-ebola-patient-42-day-countdown-to-ebola-free-begins--bb64b11de5a5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261112-kenya-discharges-last-ebola-patient-42-day-countdown-to-ebola-free-begins" /><summary type="html">Kenya has discharged its last Ebola patient, who has now officially recovered. The 11 other people who had been in quarantine were also released from hospital on Wednesday, November 11, as the country began a 42-day countdown to being declared Ebola-free. FRANCE 24's Nairobi correspondent Bastien Renouil reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>COP31: Experts call for zero waste, as Africa grapples with mounting garbage</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1cc9ecc83d5783708377fb0105e40e135219ffadb660b34eadde4ef93688d187</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:58:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T10:45:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261112-cop31-experts-call-for-zero-waste-as-africa-grapples-with-mounting-garbage--72c8e8338467.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261112-cop31-experts-call-for-zero-waste-as-africa-grapples-with-mounting-garbage" /><summary type="html">As the COP31 climate summit gets under way this week in Turkey, experts are calling for zero-waste solutions to tackle Africa's growing waste crisis. As governments search for ways to address the crisis, a new report warns of a growing push for waste-to-energy incineration across the continent. FRANCE 24 spoke to Mponwe Minette, founder and executive director of Soft Power Global and a climate activist.</summary></entry><entry><title>DR Congo's Tshisekedi paves way for constitutional change</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2276c5e19b6d935cedc73366806bf7bd944c9a9b4cbc6456fef329bcf04cc2c2</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:58:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T21:39:46Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tshisekedi-paves-way-for-constitutional-change--56435e73b5e2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tshisekedi-paves-way-for-constitutional-change" /><summary type="html">In tonight's edition: A new law expanding the conditions for a constitutional referendum has ignited political tensions in DR Congo. Also, Kenya has officially declared the end of its latest Ebola outbreak. And at the COP31 climate summit, environmental advocates are warning against waste incineration, arguing that it risks locking African cities into expensive and polluting infrastructure.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Violent clashes near the Sudanese border: At least 65 dead in western Ethiopia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d36bc669f2823f53c2e7a2ef1996f829c4566965d9ee178efe9a3f722ec59892</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:58:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T12:07:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/violent-clashes-near-the-sudanese-border-at-least-65-dead-in-western-ethiopia--6607f86e7871.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/violent-clashes-near-the-sudanese-border-at-least-65-dead-in-western-ethiopia" /><summary type="html">Tom Canetti, our correspondant in Ethiopia, has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>French journalist Christophe Gleizes marks 500 days in Algerian jail</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:51b6206f39d89721eddfdd6d5b2416be6e523880a3e3ff7e688f034ecbbef475</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:58:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T10:40:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/french-journalist-christophe-gleizes-marks-500-days-in-algerian-jail--460bfcbe4732.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/french-journalist-christophe-gleizes-marks-500-days-in-algerian-jail" /><summary type="html">Having been detained for 500 days in an Algerian prison on charges of “glorifying terrorism”, French journalist Christophe Gleizes continues to serve a seven-year sentence despite an intense campaign by his family and friends and the football world. While awaiting a presidential pardon, his supporters are stepping up their media campaign to secure his release. FRANCE 24 spoke with his friend Pierre de la Saussay.</summary></entry><entry><title>Africa: Ghana waste dump poses health, environmental 'crisis'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cd71539a7d848d9fe63ef315ff989ccdf2adc8fa7d2cd957d75f0c48fbc34a73</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:58:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T09:46:14Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/africa-ghana-waste-dump-poses-health-environmental-crisis--0d839c9497ad.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa-ghana-waste-dump-poses-health-environmental-crisis" /><summary type="html">An acrid haze hung over a sprawling dump in Ghana's capital, Accra, as excavators gouged into mounds of smouldering rubbish. Thin plumes of black smoke curled from burning plastic and rubber, mingling with the rank odour of stagnant lagoon water.</summary></entry><entry><title>Boat capsizes off Senegal's northwest coast, leaving 39 dead</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:57b09e2d1e8df7af7f37c386bad2cfdfd45b10588e1a303b90fc472eadea5f71</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:58:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T01:50:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/eye-on-africa/20261111-boat-capsized-off-senegal-s-northwest-coast-leaving-39-dead--77ec7ffb578f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/eye-on-africa/20261111-boat-capsized-off-senegal-s-northwest-coast-leaving-39-dead" /><summary type="html">At least 39 people have died after a migrant boat capsized off Senegal, one of the country's deadliest migration tragedies in recent years. We try to understand why so many are still willing to put their lives at risk, with our guest Aissata Kane from the International Organization for Migration.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>South Africa's ANC suffers historic setback in local elections as coalition talks begin</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fb3cea49d4e761f1403f8ebb001d62355f886c2ddcc9420c48364289e40ff13c</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:58:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T21:54:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/eye-on-africa/20261109-south-africa-s-anc-suffers-a-historic-setback-in-local-elections-as-coalition-talks-begin--3da15ef6ee92.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/eye-on-africa/20261109-south-africa-s-anc-suffers-a-historic-setback-in-local-elections-as-coalition-talks-begin" /><summary type="html">South Africa's ruling ANC party suffers its worst-ever local election results, securing just 30 percent of the vote, as coalition talks loom. Meanwhile, former Ugandan military intelligence officer Herbert Matanda Mabonga accuses the army of secretly detaining and torturing opponents, following the release of videos that sparked national outrage. Finally, in Senegal, more than 200,000 free tickets are giving young people the chance to experience the Youth Olympic Games live on home soil, in a bid to inspire a new generation of athletes.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Migrant boat sinks off Senegal, killing at least 34 people, authorities say</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ab7a0411cfb3b29380f2e5758d93b114e786cb2166d27a1c7f9f97634ad814fc</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:58:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-08T20:40:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/africa/20261108-migrant-boat-sinks-off-senegal-killing-at-least-34-people-authorities-say--c7e270d5fde4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20261108-migrant-boat-sinks-off-senegal-killing-at-least-34-people-authorities-say" /><summary type="html">A boat carrying migrants along the hazardous Atlantic Ocean route from West Africa to Europe sank off the coast of Senegal, killed at least 34 people, authorities said Sunday. Only one survivor has so far been found, and "an indeterminate number" are still missing.</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Kenyan cult leader sentenced to 200 years in prison</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cfc2ee5dc1aabd69c041be20d056e58412164e1223eee4fc566fc1946b95913d</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:58:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T12:10:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/kenyan-cult-leader-sentenced-to-200-years-in-prison-1--17cc7592b605.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/kenyan-cult-leader-sentenced-to-200-years-in-prison-1" /><summary type="html">Kenyan cult leader Paul Mackenzie has been sentenced to 200 years in prison for the deaths of 190 children who were starved to death on his orders in Shakahola Forest. Prosecutors said he had convinced followers to fast to reach heaven before the apocalypse, with some victims beaten, buried alive or dumped in latrines. Twenty-eight accomplices have also been jailed. The case has raised serious questions about the authorities' failure to act on repeated warning signs dating back to 2017, with the death toll from the wider investigation reaching 448 confirmed bodies and around 500 suspected victims.</summary></entry><entry><title>Kenyan cult leader sentenced to 200 years in prison</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d9643dff75a3287c14fa72a3146af05fff0797771c62b537c4b26b7b53c92cf9</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:58:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T21:23:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/kenyan-cult-leader-sentenced-to-200-years-in-prison--479d3d59e388.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/kenyan-cult-leader-sentenced-to-200-years-in-prison" /><summary type="html">In tonight's edition: Cult leader Paul Mackenzie is sentenced to 200 years in prison for the murder of 190 children starved ‌to death on his orders. Also, in South Africa, activists warn that new data centres could put added pressure on already strained water and electricity supplies. Plus Senegal continues to celebrate the spirit of sport at the Youth Olympic Games.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>The human cost of recycling: Kenyan waste pickers put their health at risk</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0ba1b4d38dc72c5f8c0c847c961f5045106a7fcefae121b47ffe411d6caf978d</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:58:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T12:34:50Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/reporters/20261106-the-human-cost-of-recycling-kenyan-waste-pickers-put-their-health-at-risk--8367ce2d13bd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/reporters/20261106-the-human-cost-of-recycling-kenyan-waste-pickers-put-their-health-at-risk" /><summary type="html">Two thousand tonnes of waste are dumped every day at the Dandora landfill site in the Kenyan capital Nairobi. An army of workers then rush in to recover recyclable materials, putting their own health at risk in the process. But however hard these unsung environmental heroes work, only 7 percent of the plastic can be recycled. Our correspondents report.</summary><category term="Reporters" /></entry><entry><title>South Africa's ANC party on track to face 'nightmare' losses in municipal elections</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:65f25182cdc7c3ef13ad18d246cfd515657e507fb491c8d8ac39f685a2e478e8</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:58:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T07:15:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/africa/20261106-south-africa-anc-party-on-track-to-face-nightmare-losses-in-municipal-elections--c38994a90651.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20261106-south-africa-anc-party-on-track-to-face-nightmare-losses-in-municipal-elections" /><summary type="html">South Africa's African National Congress party could face its worst-ever election result on Friday with about a third of support after 80 percent of the votes from local government polls counted. Final results are expected by Sunday.</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Nigerian court bars opposition candidate two months before election</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8c9f77e19180f69b5281e5313709181f9779565d660229f8714b05e4a5078d55</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:58:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T21:22:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/nigeria-court-bars-opposition-candidate-two-months-before-election--30781d646246.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/nigeria-court-bars-opposition-candidate-two-months-before-election" /><summary type="html">In tonight's edition: A Nigerian court disqualifies a leading presidential candidate, adding fresh complications to the electoral process two months before the vote. Also, tens of thousands of people have fled across the border into Kenya as deadly ethnic clashes in southern Ethiopia intensify. Plus having fled conflict and violence, members of the first Refugee Youth Olympic Team are chasing Olympic dreams in Dakar.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Nobel laureate Navi Pillay on fighting violence with justice</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7c471232c2600a79a6d8362c6a6a5dec5940a55f143b92da0d0ea800a29e0f35</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:58:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T16:12:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/navi-pillay-fighting-violence-with-justice--5c93068ee314.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/navi-pillay-fighting-violence-with-justice" /><summary type="html">From the International Criminal Court (ICC) to Africa’s place in the global justice system, the stakes are high. In an exclusive interview with FRANCE 24, Nobel Peace Prize winner Navi Pillay discusses international justice. She says it must not be held hostage to political power, as US President Donald Trump targets the ICC. What does this showdown mean for Africa?</summary><category term="Across Africa" /></entry><entry><title>South Africans eager to vote as local elections put failing services in focus</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b170e744ba900586b5578d141d6c2b17707d5f9dbf079c2f8553918b2bc950f0</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:58:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T10:48:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261105-south-africans-eager-to-vote-as-local-elections-put-failing-services-in-focus--3584f253c1f1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261105-south-africans-eager-to-vote-as-local-elections-put-failing-services-in-focus" /><summary type="html">South Africans voted on Wednesday, November 4, in local elections. Nearly 30 million people were eligible to cast their ballots, with corruption, failing infrastructure and the deterioration of essential services among the key issues shaping the vote. FRANCE 24's correspondent Eunice Masson reports from the ground.</summary></entry><entry><title>Sudan accuses Ethiopia of allowing RSF drone launches from its territory</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:293481554acf27688eb1de7870f06e8a0cc7f1118d65eef4e0058aa879a6c431</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:58:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T10:42:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261105-sudan-accuses-ethiopia-of-allowing-rsf-drone-launches-from-its-territory--8c8da3e75c7a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261105-sudan-accuses-ethiopia-of-allowing-rsf-drone-launches-from-its-territory" /><summary type="html">Sudan accused Ethiopia of allowing the paramilitary Rapid Support Forces (RSF) to launch drones from its territory. What does this allegation reveal about the RSF's military capabilities and foreign backing? FRANCE 24 spoke to Ali Mahmoud Ali, a Sudan researcher at ACLED, the Armed Conflict Location &amp; Event Data Project, which monitors conflicts worldwide.</summary></entry><entry><title>Ethiopian families fleeing conflict face difficulties with food access</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:47a45c693881585e01d394212953b5bfb0acad18b6932c4ee206f8f4b729cd05</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:58:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T10:38:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261105-ethiopian-families-fleeing-conflict-face-difficulties-with-food-access--4c415309d324.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261105-ethiopian-families-fleeing-conflict-face-difficulties-with-food-access" /><summary type="html">A renewed conflict in Ethiopia has led to the displacement of thousands of civilians. But after years of war in the country and heavy budget cuts, humanitarian organisations have all but left many of the camps for internally displaced people, leaving many without food or health care. FRANCE 24's correspondent Tom Canetti reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>South Africans vote in key municipal elections</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:25a66d58c2733e096233d02f0821e12688ea19de1a96352c4059e78ab6812a25</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:58:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T21:26:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/south-africans-vote-in-key-municipal-elections--157bcd2b0585.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/south-africans-vote-in-key-municipal-elections" /><summary type="html">In tonight's edition: South Africa's ruling ANC party faces a crucial test as millions vote to elect municipal governments. Also, Ethiopia has expelled six Sudanese diplomats amid accusations it's allowing the paramilitary RSF to launch drone strikes from its territory. Plus an ongoing humanitarian crisis deepens in Ethiopia, where renewed fighting has displaced thousands.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>DR Congo residents sue Chinese mining giant for widespread pollution</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bc036dd1834ee8d4047e6b2ecaf0d1307dd0e389edf5e378ffa47243dcbd520f</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:58:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T10:22:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261104-dr-congo-residents-sue-chinese-mining-giant-for-widespread-pollution--3060f906634c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261104-dr-congo-residents-sue-chinese-mining-giant-for-widespread-pollution" /><summary type="html">In Kolwezi, the mining capital of the Democratic Republic of Congo, local residents are suing a huge Chinese mine and the government for environmental pollution. It will be one of the most important cases the country has seen. FRANCE 24's correspondent Emmet Livingstone reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>30 million South Africans registered to vote across nine provinces</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:179e7a83a3279456463cb83a08ee1f3c622ea16ee505292ac71d693c5ae68684</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:58:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T10:20:37Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261104-30-million-south-africans-registered-to-vote-across-nine-provinces--878860fdbba8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261104-30-million-south-africans-registered-to-vote-across-nine-provinces" /><summary type="html">In South Africa, around 30 million people have registered to cast their votes across the country's nine provinces. The economy is at the forefront of the November 4 local elections. The spotlight is on Gauteng, a province long plagued by governance challenges. FRANCE 24's correspondent Eunice Masson reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Sudanese Arab refugees face hostility and distrust after fleeing to Chad</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0c2d9edff73c675e5e7d5c151e1c3246288e53d90db245ba3061dafad9d71f94</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:58:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T10:18:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261104-sudanese-arab-refugees-face-hostility-and-distrust-after-fleeing-to-chad--6a0e74aca0b3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261104-sudanese-arab-refugees-face-hostility-and-distrust-after-fleeing-to-chad" /><summary type="html">Thousands of Arab Sudanese who have arrived in Chad after fleeing fighting at home are facing mistrust and hostility from fellow Sudanese refugees. Fighters linked to the Rapid Support Forces, whose ranks are largely drawn from Sudan’s Arab communities, have been accused of repeatedly targeting civilians from other ethnic groups. FRANCE 24's Harold Girard reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Washington excludes South Africa and Rwanda from US duty-free trade deal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:67a1e8ca3fb717c8268d26f75275e1ed81414f67bff75308758f0a21efbb59b9</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:58:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T10:15:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261104-washington-excludes-south-africa-and-rwanda-from-us-duty-free-trade-deal--4bfd48eab3d8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261104-washington-excludes-south-africa-and-rwanda-from-us-duty-free-trade-deal" /><summary type="html">South African and Rwandan exporters are weighing potential job losses and squeezed margins after Washington decided to exclude them from the AGOA program, the African Growth and Opportunity Act, ending the countries' duty-free access to the US market. Economists warned against "alarmist" reactions to the exclusion and argue the broader economic fallout will likely be limited.</summary></entry><entry><title>South Africa braces for some job losses as AGOA ends</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3a71e655de48f8f08eeadd9e1239c21a958cce0da323cbb7ce903fb562f4a8be</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:58:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T21:18:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/south-africa-braces-for-some-job-losses-as-agoa-ends--b18e322d68f6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/south-africa-braces-for-some-job-losses-as-agoa-ends" /><summary type="html">In tonight's edition: Rwanda and South Africa will lose their duty-free access to the US market after being excluded from the AGOA trade programme. Also, South Africans head to the polls amid water shortages and frustration with local services. Plus in DR Congo's mining capital Kolwezi, residents are taking on one of the country's largest Chinese-owned mines, accusing it of poisoning their environment.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Senegal's opposition-dominated parliament rejects revised budget bill</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9253760d790d29982425fb6ffc2630ece3474634490393dea6b2901aff6db4a1</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:58:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T12:40:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/africa/20261103-senegal-powerful-opposition-rejects-crucial-budget-bill--942d392c755d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20261103-senegal-powerful-opposition-rejects-crucial-budget-bill" /><summary type="html">Senegal's powerful opposition party Pastef led by former presidential candidate Ousmane Sonko on Tuesday rejected a revised version of the country's budget, leaving the west African nation's new bailout programme with the International Monetary Fund hanging in the balance.</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Uganda withdraws its troops from Somalia as fight against rebels persists</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d77cf4c7f067ed7474cfae12253b808edf2935f043b0fb31023070f992aaf487</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:58:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T11:50:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-uganda-withdraws-its-troops-from-somalia-as-fight-against-rebels-persists--878da3c15104.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-uganda-withdraws-its-troops-from-somalia-as-fight-against-rebels-persists" /><summary type="html">Kampala announced on Monday it had begun pulling its troops out of Somalia. Uganda was the first country to send deployments to help Mogadishu when the African Union set up an international military mission in 2007 to battle al-Shabab extremist rebels. But what is prompting Kampala to withdraw its troops now, as the battle against the militants continues? FRANCE 24’s Georga Calvin Smith is joined by Horn of Africa geopolitical analyst Anwar Abdifatah Bashir.</summary></entry><entry><title>South Africans demand security and basic services as they vote in local elections</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c12f86d334f756ae3c5ed7a761e71ecaf42351061f40f0be454a6ae7c02ff4af</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:58:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T11:39:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-south-africans-demand-security-and-basic-services-as-they-vote-in-local-elections--7b95b95f6073.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-south-africans-demand-security-and-basic-services-as-they-vote-in-local-elections" /><summary type="html">High crime rates and a lack of basic services are causing concern among many of South Africa’s 29 million registered voters. Water shortages and unreliable electricity supplies have also become symbols of municipal failures, angering voters and eroding support for the ruling African National Congress. The municipal elections on November 4 will offer a glimpse into whether these frustrations are shifting political loyalties.</summary></entry></feed>
